{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"New Jersey Fair Chance in Housing Act (criminal record screening limits)","requirement":"Housing providers may not ask about an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, except for methamphetamine manufacture on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex offender registration. After a conditional offer, they may consider only specified convictions within look-back periods, and may withdraw the offer only after an individualized assessment with written notice, an opportunity to appeal, and prior written disclosure of their criminal-history criteria.","key_value":"Ban on criminal record inquiries before a conditional offer; look-back limits of 6 years (first-degree), 4 years (second/third-degree) and 1 year (fourth-degree) after a conditional offer","status":"in_force","effective_date":"2022-01-01","end_date":null,"citation":"P.L.2021, c.110 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-52 to 46:8-64)","coverage_conditions":"Applies to housing providers offering rental dwelling units for residential purposes.","exemptions":"Excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2","c3"],"primary":"c3","title":"NJ Law Against Discrimination: source of lawful income / rent payment protection in housing","requirement":"The NJ Law Against Discrimination prohibits housing discrimination based on the source of lawful income or source of lawful rent or mortgage payment a tenant uses. A landlord cannot deny a lawful recipient of a Section 8 HUD voucher the right to rent an apartment based solely on that source of income.","key_value":"Cannot deny rental based solely on Section 8 voucher / lawful source of income","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 10:5-1 et seq.; N.J.S.A. 10:5-12(g), (h)","coverage_conditions":"Applies to the sale or rental of all property, including open land, for business or residential purposes.","exemptions":"Rental of a single apartment or flat in a two-family dwelling where the other unit is occupied by the owner as a residence at the time of rental; rental of a room or rooms by the owner or occupant of a one-family dwelling occupied as a residence at the time of rental; preference given to persons of the same religion by a religious organization; residences planned exclusively for and occupied by one sex.","coverage_from":"c3","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
